notes.body:
Here is what it looks like on one example taken from https://wiki.wireshark.org/Lua/Examples.

Without Lua Language Server:

![without-lua-ls.png](/uploads/ec010c4647d28bc5d8de406fb17bcc39/without-lua-ls.png){width=509 height=494}

With Lua Language Server but without wslua support, you get nice colors but also errors when you use wslua items:

![with-lua-ls-without-wslua-support.png](/uploads/1ab9fa29fc9150af552a0fe428137e09/with-lua-ls-without-wslua-support.png){width=512 height=407}

With Lua Language Server and wslua support, you get documentation on hover and autocompletion:

![with-lua-ls-with-wslua-support.png](/uploads/c18c3792e499a773b7451988ae80c891/with-lua-ls-with-wslua-support.png){width=513 height=378}

The Lua globals registered in `epan/wslua/init_wslua.c` are not supported since they are not wrapped with the macros used to parse the code for generating AsciiDoc files.

I'm trying to figure out if I can do something relevant for these globals, but it might be better to leave it out for another merge request (if this one is of interest for you, of course).

